{"data": [{"author_id": "14096763", "created_at": "2026-10-31T14:05:37.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116532045530984733"], "id": "2116532045530984733", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 2, "impression_count": 18432, "like_count": 143, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 12, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "Just a reminder that at 1:30 today, a bunch of regulars are going to be at the Tompkins Square exercise bars (northeast corner). Please come out and say hi and do a few chin-ups with us. They’re good for you.", "url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2116532045530984733"}, {"author_id": "702235316812275712", "created_at": "2026-10-31T13:41:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116525849251914149"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 26, "id": "156016878", "start": 15, "username": "Neil_Irwin"}, {"end": 36, "id": "800707492346925056", "start": 30, "username": "axios"}], "urls": [{"description": "More of employers' overall spending on worker compensation is going to health benefits, leaving less for wages and salaries.", "display_url": "axios.com/2026/10/30/hea…", "end": 158, "expanded_url": "https://www.axios.com/2026/10/30/health-care-wages-employment-cost-index", "images": [{"height": 768, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2116199860231651328/FC0i6X-U?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1366}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2116199860231651328/FC0i6X-U?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 135, "status": 200, "title": "Health care is eating Americans' paychecks", "unwound_url": "https://www.axios.com/2026/10/30/health-care-wages-employment-cost-index", "url": "https://t.co/YoQAI2OBpu"}]}, "id": "2116525849251914149", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 5, "impression_count": 4492, "like_count": 22, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 3, "retweet_count": 4}, "text": "Am grateful to @Neil_Irwin at @axios for chatting with me about how surging health insurance costs are squeezing workers' pay raises.\n\nhttps://t.co/YoQAI2OBpu", "url": "https://x.com/EconBerger/status/2116525849251914149"}, {"author_id": "3512101", "created_at": "2026-10-31T13:02:34.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116516180097696203"], "id": "2116516180097696203", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 10, "impression_count": 6641, "like_count": 19, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 5, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "\"\"General Secretary Xi Jinping addressed the doubts some people have: “Does comprehensively and strictly governing the Party hinder economic and social development, or does it safeguard and promote it?”", "url": "https://x.com/niubi/status/2116516180097696203"}, {"author_id": "917683048782503937", "created_at": "2026-10-31T07:11:27.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116427817609032055"], "id": "2116427817609032055", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 8, "impression_count": 10364, "like_count": 59, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 4, "retweet_count": 15}, "text": "Caixin: \"China’s banks are being encouraged to steer more credit toward technology, green industries and small businesses. But as overall demand for loans weakens, the policy push is creating increasing competition to lend to companies that may need their money least, while some", "url": "https://x.com/michaelxpettis/status/2116427817609032055"}, {"author_id": "917683048782503937", "created_at": "2026-10-31T06:41:06.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116420177562620406"], "id": "2116420177562620406", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 6, "impression_count": 13767, "like_count": 46, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 4, "retweet_count": 11}, "text": "Xinhua: \"China's manufacturing activity moderated in October, with the PMI falling to 49.3, while high-tech and equipment manufacturing sectors maintained expansion. Large manufacturers continued to report expansion, with their PMI standing at 50.2, despite a slight decline of", "url": "https://x.com/michaelxpettis/status/2116420177562620406"}, {"author_id": "917683048782503937", "created_at": "2026-10-31T06:36:51.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116419107318866362"], "id": "2116419107318866362", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 37, "impression_count": 27164, "like_count": 249, "quote_count": 4, "reply_count": 13, "retweet_count": 37}, "text": "In a story about rising Chinese consumption Xinhua notes that in the first three quarters of 2026, \"domestic consumption contributed nearly half of economic growth, driving GDP growth up by 2.1 percentage points\".\n\nWhat it doesn't say is that excluding twice during the COVID", "url": "https://x.com/michaelxpettis/status/2116419107318866362"}, {"author_id": "702235316812275712", "created_at": "2026-10-31T02:07:06.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116351224585097400"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/inlandcaguy/st…", "end": 161, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/inlandcaguy/status/2116321802662338580", "start": 138, "url": "https://t.co/KatkLQHdxO"}]}, "id": "2116351224585097400", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 3215, "like_count": 7, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2116321802662338580", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "I agree that Patrick Stewart was perfect for “The Inner Light”…\n\nOTOH I can’t imagine the TNG ensemble pulling off “Far Beyond the Stars” https://t.co/KatkLQHdxO", "url": "https://x.com/EconBerger/status/2116351224585097400"}, {"author_id": "702235316812275712", "created_at": "2026-10-31T00:14:12.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116322811082072295"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/EconBerger/sta…", "end": 59, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/EconBerger/status/2116315630559490340", "start": 36, "url": "https://t.co/F1ErUHcWxA"}]}, "id": "2116322811082072295", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3213, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2116315630559490340", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "TNG : DS9 :: Lou Reed : David Bowie https://t.co/F1ErUHcWxA", "url": "https://x.com/EconBerger/status/2116322811082072295"}, {"author_id": "702235316812275712", "created_at": "2026-10-30T23:56:04.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116318248191066463"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/MikeVorkunov/s…", "end": 304, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/MikeVorkunov/status/2115892935648563359", "start": 281, "url": "https://t.co/V6B2tRmvFj"}]}, "id": "2116318248191066463", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 35, "impression_count": 22436, "like_count": 171, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 15, "retweet_count": 12}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2115892935648563359", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "My general feeling about this is:\n\n1/ It's hard to find a job right now because marginal labor demand is weak and only slowly recovering\n\n2/ this \"can't talk to a real person\" is a screening friction that's been introduced to compensate for a massive decline in application costs. https://t.co/V6B2tRmvFj", "url": "https://x.com/EconBerger/status/2116318248191066463"}, {"author_id": "702235316812275712", "created_at": "2026-10-30T23:45:40.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116315630559490340"], "id": "2116315630559490340", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 4374, "like_count": 6, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "TNG : DS9 :: Chuck Berry : The Beatles", "url": "https://x.com/EconBerger/status/2116315630559490340"}, {"author_id": "30034124", "created_at": "2026-10-30T23:09:01.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116306406475223245"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "Following years of preparation, the new result from the Short-Baseline Near Detector improves neutrino interaction modeling, paving the way for the Deep Underground Neutrino Experiment.", "display_url": "news.fnal.gov/2026/10/the-sb…", "end": 238, "expanded_url": "https://news.fnal.gov/2026/10/the-sbnd-collaboration-releases-first-neutri